 spring season off right with Scotts® Turf Builder® Halts® Crabgrass Preventer with Lawn Food. This pre-emergent weed killer plus fertilizer stops crabgrass before it invades and protects all season long. It also prevents other listed grassy and broadleaf weeds, including barnyard grass, foxtail, poa annua, chickweed, and oxalis. The added fertilizer feeds for a fast green-up after winter and helps build strong, deep grass roots. Apply Scotts® Turf Builder® Halts® Crabgrass Preventer with Lawn Food in early spring (prior to 3rd or 4th mowing) when your lawn is dry and before temperatures are regularly in the 80s. For best results, the lawn should receive ¼ to ½ inch of water from rainfall or watering within 2-3 days after application. We recommend using a Scotts® spreader to apply this product. For Scotts® broadcast/rotary spreaders, use a setting of 3. For Scotts® drop spreaders, use a setting of 6. Do NOT apply to Dichondra and Bentgrass. This product controls crabgrass in its early stages of growth. It does not control mature crabgrass and other existing weeds. One 13.35 lb. bag of Scotts® Turf Builder® Halts® Crabgrass Preventer with Lawn Food covers 5,000 sq. ft.                  From the Manufacturer               Use Scotts Turf Builder with HALTS Crab Grass Preventer to prevent crab grass all season long and feed for a fast green-up after winter. One application creates a barrier over the entire lawn to prevent crab grass and other grassy weeds from sprouting.Turf Builder builds a thick, green lawn and should be applied to a dry lawn in early spring. For use on established bermuda grass (non-overseeded), St. Augustine grass, centipede grass, bahia grass, zoysia grass, tall fescue, fine fescue, Kentucky blue grass, perennial rye grass, and blends of these grasses. Do not use on dichondra and bent grass lawns. Coverage: 5,000 square feet. Fertilizer analysis: 30-0-4.", "isFreeShipping": true}	2026-03-25 12:53:01.926251	amazon	\N
